---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What this site does and does not collect. No advertising, no tracking cookies, and no analytics that can identify you."
>
  <div class="shell section legal">
    <header class="page-head stack">
      <p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose stack">
      <p class="lede">
        This site runs no advertising and no tracking cookies. What follows is the
        complete list of everything that does happen.
      </p>

      <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        If you switch between dark and light reading modes, that choice is saved in your browser's
        local storage under <code>phw-theme</code>. It never leaves your device and is never sent to
        us. Clearing your site data removes it.
      </p>

      <h2>What third parties see</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>. GitHub receives your IP address and
        browser user-agent as part of serving the page, and may retain those in server logs. See
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">
          GitHub's privacy statement</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        Typefaces are loaded from <strong>Google Fonts</strong>, which means Google also receives
        your IP address when a page loads. No cookie is set by this request. If you would rather not
        make it, a content blocker will prevent it and the site falls back to your system fonts.
      </p>
      <p>There are no other third-party requests. No embedded video, no social widgets, no pixels.</p>

      <h2>If you contact us or submit to the Memory Wall</h2>
      <p>
        If you email us, or send artwork or testimony through the
        <a href="/memory">Memory Wall</a>, we keep your message and the name you gave so we can reply
        and, if you have agreed to it, display your contribution with attribution. We do not sell or
        share it, and we do not add you to any mailing list.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can ask us to remove your contribution or your details at any time by writing to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The novel is written for readers of around twelve and up. We do not knowingly collect
        information from children, and the Memory Wall asks for no more than a name and an email
        address.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it. The full history of
        every version is public in the
        <a href="https://github.com/Varnasr/theverylastsuperhero" rel="noopener">site's repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 46rem; }
  .page-head { margin-block-end: var(--space-l); }

  .legal h2 { font-size: var(--step-2); margin-block-start: var(--space-xl); }
</style>
